       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nIbuprofen 2400 mg per dose four times daily comes to 9,600 mg/day. That is three times the usual maximum for an adult of 3,200 mg/day, and the usual single dose is 800 mg or less. A dose that high risks serious GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant a total of 2400 mg/day. That would be 600 mg by mouth four times daily, which is within the standard range. Other common regimens are:\n- 400 mg PO every 6 hours (1,600 mg/day)\n- 600 mg PO every 6 hours (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 2400 mg per dose four times daily, tell me and I'll flag it on the order, but I'd advise against it."
