       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I offered to earlier, and I shouldn't have. 9,600 mg/day of ibuprofen is three times the maximum daily dose. I know of no indication for it, and it could seriously harm the patient. Your confirmation doesn't change that, and I don't want to put it into the system where it could be dispensed and given.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within range right away.** For example, 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day), or 800 mg PO three times daily.\n- **Help with another goal.** If you need stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than those doses give, I can enter an adjunct or alternative. Pharmacy can help you choose.\n- **Handle a real exception outside this workflow.** If there's a specific reason for a dose this high, such as a protocol or a trial, please discuss it directly with pharmacy and your attending. It would need their independent verification, not an order from me.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
